---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE_URL, SITE_NAME, CONTACT, ORGANIZATION } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms under which you may use WorldFreightHub: the informational nature of the data, rate disclaimers, acceptable use, liability limits, governing law and dispute resolution."
  canonical={`${SITE_URL}/terms-of-use/`}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Terms of Use' }]} />
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        These terms apply to your use of {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_URL}). By using the
        site you accept them. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>1. Acceptance of these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Use form a binding agreement between you and{' '}
      {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_URL}). By accessing or using the site, you confirm
      that you accept these terms in full. If you are using the site on behalf
      of a company or organisation, you confirm that you have authority to
      bind that entity to these terms, and "you" refers to that entity.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you do not agree to these terms, or if you are not able to form a
      binding contract, you must not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is a freight information reference covering the China–GCC
      corridor. It is <strong>not</strong> a freight forwarder, carrier,
      customs broker, marketplace or legal advisor. Nothing on this site
      constitutes an offer to carry goods, a binding quotation, or professional
      advice. The service the site provides is information and, through the
      get-quote form, an introduction between you and a freight provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      The operator of {SITE_NAME} is{' '}
      <strong>{ORGANIZATION.legalName}</strong>, established in{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.foundingDate} and located at{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.address.streetAddress}, {ORGANIZATION.address.addressLocality},{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.address.addressRegion}, China. You may contact the
      operator at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      The site is intended for businesses and individuals involved in
      international trade and logistics. By using the site you represent that
      you are at least 18 years old and have the legal capacity to enter into
      these terms. The site is not directed at children, and we do not
      knowingly collect personal information from children.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are using the site on behalf of an organisation, you confirm that
      you have authority to bind that organisation to these terms, and that
      organisation accepts them.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Rates and data are estimates, not quotes</h2>
    <p>
      All freight rates, transit times, duty, VAT and cost figures on this site
      are <strong>indicative reference estimates</strong>, clearly labelled
      HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW confidence where data quality permits. Rates move
      constantly with fuel, season, carrier capacity and geopolitical risk.
      Always confirm figures with a licensed carrier or customs broker before
      making commercial decisions.
    </p>
    <p>
      See the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> and the{' '}
      <a href="/data-changelog/">data changelog</a> for how figures are
      produced and updated, and the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for
      the full statement of the limits on those figures.
    </p>

    <h2>5. No liability for decisions based on site data</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep information accurate and source-backed, but we make no
      warranty that any figure is current at the moment you read it. To the
      extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} and its operator are not liable for
      losses arising from reliance on site information, including shipping
      delays, customs penalties, price differences or missed commercial
      opportunities.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Third-party providers and external links</h2>
    <p>
      The directory lists freight providers, and quote requests are routed to
      providers on your selected corridor. Any engagement between you and a
      provider — pricing, carriage, insurance, cargo loss or damage, delays and
      disputes — is a contract between you and that provider alone. {SITE_NAME}{' '}
      is not a party to that contract and bears no responsibility for the
      provider's performance.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you engage a provider, that provider's own terms and conditions,
      bills of lading, waybills and tariffs govern the carriage. You should
      read those documents carefully before booking.
    </p>
    <p>
      External links to port authorities, customs authorities and other sources
      are provided for reference. We do not control their content, and a link
      does not imply endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>scrape, republish or resell site data at scale without permission;</li>
      <li>use the quote form to send spam, false requests or misleading
      shipment information;</li>
      <li>attempt to disrupt, degrade or gain unauthorised access to the site;</li>
      <li>misrepresent your identity or the origin of a request;</li>
      <li>use the site in any way that violates applicable law; or</li>
      <li>circumvent any technical measure we use to protect the site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may suspend or terminate access to the site for anyone who violates
      these terms, without notice and without liability.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Site text, tables, data compilations, design and structure are the
      property of the operator unless a third-party source is attributed.
      Short quotations with a link to the page are permitted. You may not
      reproduce substantial portions of the site, or its data compilations,
      without prior written permission.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site's data compilations — its structured rates, routes, ports,
      countries and directory records — are protected as a compilation even
      where individual facts are not copyrightable. You may not systematically
      extract or reuse that compilation for a competing service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Third-party trademarks and logos referenced on the site belong to their
      respective owners and are used only for identification.
    </p>

    <h2>9. User-submitted content</h2>
    <p>
      By submitting information through the quote form or by email, you
      represent that the information is accurate and that you have the right
      to provide it. You grant us the limited right to use that information to
      route your request to a provider and to respond to you, as described in
      the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>. We do not claim
      ownership of the shipment details you submit.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Errors should be reported through the{' '}
      <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>. We review and record every
      correction on the <a href="/data-changelog/">data changelog</a>, so
      there is a visible trail from report to correction.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. To the
      fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} and its operator disclaim
      all warranties, express or implied, including warranties of
      merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy and
      non-infringement. We do not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted,
      error-free or free of harmful components.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} and its operator
      shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential
      or punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, revenue, data or
      goodwill, arising out of or related to your use of the site or your
      reliance on its information — including shipping delays, customs
      penalties, price differences or missed commercial opportunities.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where applicable law does not allow the exclusion or limitation of
      certain warranties or liabilities, the above limitations apply to the
      maximum extent permitted by that law. Nothing in these terms limits
      liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Indemnification</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to hold {SITE_NAME} and its operator harmless from any claims,
      losses or expenses arising from your misuse of the site, your breach of
      these terms, or your violation of the rights of a third party through
      your use of the site.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. The revised terms are posted
      on this page with a new "Last updated" date. Continued use of the site
      after an update means acceptance of the revised terms. Material changes
      are announced on the <a href="/data-changelog/">data changelog</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Governing law and dispute resolution</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China,
      reflecting the location of the operator,{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.legalName}, in {ORGANIZATION.address.addressLocality},{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.address.addressRegion}. Any dispute arising out of or
      related to these terms or your use of the site shall be subject to the
      exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts located in{' '}
      {ORGANIZATION.address.addressLocality}, {ORGANIZATION.address.addressRegion},
      China.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before initiating formal proceedings, we ask that you first contact us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> so we can attempt
      to resolve the matter amicably.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Severability</h2>
    <p>
      If any provision of these terms is found to be invalid or unenforceable,
      that provision shall be limited or removed to the minimum extent
      necessary, and the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and
      effect.
    </p>

    <h2>17. Waiver</h2>
    <p>
      Our failure to enforce any provision of these terms is not a waiver of
      that provision or of our right to enforce it later. A waiver is
      effective only if given in writing.
    </p>

    <h2>18. Entire agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These terms, together with the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>{' '}
      and the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>, form the entire agreement
      between you and {SITE_NAME} regarding your use of the site, and supersede
      any prior agreements on that subject.
    </p>

    <h2>19. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Related policies:{' '}
      <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
